## Available
  1: the Newcomer - a dormant, not-yet-introduced one-star Hero whose complete visible identity arrives with their first summon while their nature and past emerge through play
     Choose this Hero's name and visible appearance when you join. You control their body, speech, and choices from the moment they are summoned, and you alone can read their private System windows.
  2: the Master - the unreachable will that summons, prepares, deploys, invests in, and discards the party from the far side of the glass, then watches while deployed Heroes act for themselves
     In the lobby and before deployment, act through exact interface choices: summon Heroes; build or upgrade facilities; spend resources; choose the floor, roster, and loadout; train, equip, promote, bench, synthesize, or transform units. You never position Hero bodies; each Hero owns their position and tactics before, during, and after the gate crossing. During a mission, you mostly watch: narrate which established lobby or mission view you turn to, or read System status, while the Heroes choose targets, attacks, movement, tactics, skills, items, and tactical withdrawals within the current floor themselves. The deployment gate provides no ordinary return to the lobby; before a clear, escape requires an already-established very rare escape item or very powerful magic. Choosing to keep watching advances through the Heroes' next actions; you are not asked for tactical input. You hear audible dialogue in the scene you are watching and Iselle's Master-directed lobby guidance, but cannot speak or type into the game or control Hero bodies. The direct first-floor arrival has no Iselle briefing or management handoff.
  3: Halcyon - six-star champion of a wealthy, far-along rival Master; the face of what a funded lobby looks like
     Control Halcyon's body, speech, and choices inside the distant Gilded March. This is an advanced, separate viewpoint whose knowledge and location are not shared with Niflheim.

